      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T18:58:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was assuming that this flag would control the existence of the PAGE_SIZE macro, but that\u0027s not what aosp/2675944 does.  Is there a reason this can\u0027t just be `ifndef PAGE_SIZE`?",
      "parentUuid": "1625e06e_f4217162",
      "revId": "9095de28262a4a4e0cd872631b69a814562ea6b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "290efa4e_40db69c8",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1889140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T19:05:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This C/C++ flag __BIONIC_NO_PAGE_SIZE_MACRO will be used in ART, Perfetto, etc. Basically in all the places where PAGE_SIZE is used.\n\nFor 4k targets, PAGE_SIZE will have the value 4096. For page size agnostic targets, PAGE_SIZE will have the function call getpagesize().\n\nIn nutshell, PAGE_SIZE is always defined.",
      "parentUuid": "033c9465_4acbed93",
      "revId": "9095de28262a4a4e0cd872631b69a814562ea6b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "578ffb15_729a480d",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T19:07:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, PAGE_SIZE is still defined when __BIONIC_NO_PAGE_SIZE_MACRO is.\n\nOne thing though, we don\u0027t actually need to make any changes on host or set __BIONIC_NO_PAGE_SIZE_MACRO on host. It would be okay to set it on device builds only. We can completely ignore host things or keep them at 4k.\n\nIs there a place you would recommend Colin to set this for device?",
      "parentUuid": "033c9465_4acbed93",
      "revId": "9095de28262a4a4e0cd872631b69a814562ea6b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
